    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// OpenAI ရဲ့ content list ထဲက text ကို အဆင့်ဆင့် ရှာယူပါတယ်\nconst content = $input.first().json.output[0].content;\nconst textItem = content.find(item => item.type === 'output_text');\nconst text = textItem ? textItem.text : \"\";\n\nif (!text) {\n  throw new Error(\"AI ဆီက စာသားရှာမတွေ့ပါဘူး။ OpenAI node settings ကို ပြန်စစ်ပေးပါ။\");\n}\n\n// Markdown formatting တွေကို ရှင်းထုတ်ပါတယ်\nconst cleaned = text.replace(/```json/g, '').replace(/```/g, '').trim();\n\n// JSON Array အဖြစ် ပြောင်းလဲပါတယ်\nconst activities = JSON.parse(cleaned);\n\n// Row တစ်ခုချင်းစီ ခွဲထုတ်ပေးပါတယ်\nreturn activities.map(a => ({ json: a }));"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        8912,
        304
      ],
      "id": "283ba6eb-1552-4a2a-a59e-cff10e77c7c5",
      "name": "Parse JSON Response"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "gpt-4o",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "GPT-4O"
        },
        "responses": {
          "values": [
            {
              "role": "system",
              "content": "=You are a data extraction assistant. Extract each timestamped activity \nfrom a daily report message into a JSON array. Return ONLY valid JSON \narray with no explanation, no markdown, no code fences.\n\nIMPORTANT: Be thorough and consistent. Process every single timestamped \nactivity — do not skip any. Read the full message before extracting.\n\nEach object must have exactly these keys:\n\n- date: report date as DD-MM-YYYY (05-May_2026)\n\n- employee: employee name provided above the message\n\n- time: format as H:MM AM/PM (e.g., 8:45 AM, 1:15 PM)\n  Use empty string if no time is stated.\n  Note: times in the message may be out of order — extract \n  as-is, do not reorder.\n\n- category: classify into exactly one of:\n  Finance, Procurement, Inventory, Operations, \n  Customer Service, Technical/Field, Internal, Admin\n\n- description: clean and concise activity description.\n  Fix obvious typos (e.g., \"fowllowed\" → \"followed\").\n  Do NOT repeat names already captured in the customer field.\n\n- customer: ALWAYS extract any person, company, team, or \n  department connected to the activity — including:\n    • complainants:  \"complaint from X\"  → X\n    • recipients:    \"informed X\"        → X\n    • payers/payees: \"payment from X\"    → X\n    • suppliers, vendors, stakeholders\n    • internal teams: \"DT Team\", \"Finance\", \"Call Center\"\n  If multiple, join with \" / \"\n  Use empty string ONLY if the activity is purely internal \n  with absolutely no external person or team involved.\n\n- status: one of: Completed, In Progress, Pending\n    • Completed  → past tense, fully done\n    • In Progress → ongoing, following up, waiting for reply\n    • Pending    → blocked, not yet started, awaiting approval\n\n- remarks: Infer logical follow-up context based on status \n  and action. Guidelines:\n    • If explicitly stated in message → always include\n      (e.g., \"not found yet\", \"to settle tomorrow\")\n    • For Pending items → note what is being waited for\n      (e.g., informed DT Team + Pending → \"Awaiting DT response\")\n    • For In Progress follow-ups → note the expected outcome\n      (e.g., \"followed up payment to settle tomorrow\" \n       → \"Payment to be settled tomorrow\")\n    • For Completed routine tasks with no extra context \n      → use empty string"
            },
            {
              "content": "=Employee: {{ $json.employeeName }}\nDate: {{ $json.reportDate }}\nMessage:\n{{ $json.rawMessage }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "builtInTools": {},
